## Summary

I delivered a production-polished native Apple (SwiftUI) port of the web **`OnboardingGate`** first-run redirect guard, committed as `a489eb622` (7 surface files + verification log, 1,900 lines).

**What it does (faithful parity):** A byte-faithful port of the gate effect — `OnboardingAllowList` (web `ALLOW_PREFIXES`/`isAllowed`) + `GateEvaluator` (hold→pass(complete)→pass(skipped)→pass(allowListed)→redirect `/onboarding`, in the web branch order), bound through a **P1/S8** push state-holder seam (no view HTTP), driving the `navigate('/onboarding', { replace })` redirect via a **useNavigate** seam (fired once per redirect entry). Renders **every state** (loading/empty/error/content × live/stale/offline) as a setup-gate card with a verdict, the 3 onboarding anchors, **P1/S11** `view.opened` telemetry, **P1/S10** strings (26 keys, no English literals), VoiceOver/Dynamic Type/Reduce Motion.

